preferred-citation:
  type: conference-paper
  title: "QUANTA: A Fine-Grained Dataset and Benchmark for Arabic Machine-Translation Error Analysis"
  authors: *authors
  year: 2026
  collection-title: "Proceedings of the Second Arabic Natural Language Processing Conference (ArabicNLP 2026)"
abstract: >-
  Raqeeb is a community toolkit for fine-grained Arabic machine translation
  error detection. It comprises five artifacts: the Mizan 23-class taxonomy,
  the QUANTA dataset (9,032 instances), the ETCA cross-vendor audit protocol,
  the Raqbench benchmark with the released Raqeeb classifier (Gold macro-F1 =
  0.614), and a dual-annotator validation protocol. A controlled ablation shows
  anchor-validated real data is ~12x more sample-efficient than size-matched
  synthetic data.
